+# Feature Specification: Reject invalid input
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-11 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Screens pass raw user input to the list; reject invalid input with a clear error.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Bad input is refused with a clear reason (Priority: P1)
+
+When a task is added, renamed or tagged with invalid input, the operation fails with an error whose message says what is wrong, and the list is left unchanged.
+
+**Independent Test**: try each invalid input on add, rename and tag; check the error, then check the list is unchanged.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** any list, **When** adding a task with an empty or spaces-only title, **Then** it is rejected and nothing is added.
+2. **Given** any list, **When** a title (after trimming) exceeds 120 characters, **Then** it is rejected; exactly 120 is accepted.
+3. **Given** any list, **When** a priority is not `low`, `normal` or `high`, **Then** it is rejected.
+4. **Given** any list, **When** a tag is empty or contains a space, **Then** it is rejected (on add with tags, and on tag).
+5. **Given** a task, **When** renamed to an invalid title, **Then** it is rejected and the task keeps its title and update time.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: Titles that are empty or only spaces are rejected.
+- **FR-002**: Titles longer than 120 characters (after trimming) are rejected.
+- **FR-003**: Priorities other than low, normal, high are rejected, even when passed untyped by a screen.
+- **FR-004**: Tags that are empty or contain a space are rejected.
+- **FR-005**: Checks apply on add (title, priority, every tag), rename (new title) and tag (tag).
+- **FR-006**: Each error has a distinct code for programs and a message naming the problem. A rejected operation changes nothing, including ids.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Whitespace in tags means any whitespace character. Valid input behaves as before.
+- Invalid input is reported before a missing task or a duplicate title.
+
+## Success Criteria
+
+- **SC-001**: Every invalid case above yields a failed result with a message naming the problem; the list is identical afterwards.
